# Build-context exclusions for every image in deploy/docker/.
#
# All four Dockerfiles use the MONOREPO ROOT as their context, so without this
# file the daemon would upload Rust target/ trees and node_modules/ on every
# build — slow, and a way for local artefacts or secrets to reach an image
# layer. Anything the builds genuinely need is listed as an exception below.

# ── Build outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/
control-plane/vendor/
control-plane/coverage.out
control-plane/*.test
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# ── Secrets — never let these into a layer ───────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
.git-credentials

# ── VCS / CI / editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.editorconfig
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# ── Docs and non-build assets ────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md
docs/
deploy/monitoring/
deploy/helm/
deploy/compose/
infra/
tests/load/
fuzz/
ai-training/
**/*.proptest-regressions

# ── Exceptions: required by the builds ───────────────────────────────────────
# The dashboard image needs the committed lockfile for `npm ci`.
!aether-x-dashboard/package-lock.json
# The Rust images need the workspace lockfile for `cargo build --locked`.
!Cargo.lock
